<title>USA: ComEd trims Quad Cities 2 nuke output.</title>
<headline>ComEd trims Quad Cities 2 nuke output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison Co (ComEd) reduced output over the weekend at its 789 megawatt (MW) Quad Cities nuclear generating unit 2 for valve repairs, Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Monday.</p>
<p>In its daily status report, NRC said ComEd planned to trim operations at the station, in Cordova, Ill., to about 200 MW to stop a leak at a water cleanup system containment isolation valve.</p>
<p>The neighboring Quad Cities unit 1, also rated at 789 MW, was producing at full capacity, NRC said.</p>
<p>Commonwealth Edison is a subsidiary of Unicom Corp.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk 212-859-1622</p>
